<node id="11134456" title="Re: Using 'keys' on a list (updated)" created="2021-06-29 13:13:50" updated="2021-06-29 13:13:50" _doctext_mode="strict"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;You can use &lt;c&gt;pairkeys&lt;/c&gt; from [doc://List::Util], i.e. &lt;c&gt;say for pairkeys f;&lt;/c&gt; works fine. You'll need [doc://List::Util] 1.29 for this function, which is part of the Perl core since 5.20, or you can get it from CPAN.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Update:&lt;/b&gt; [tybalt89] [id://11134459|makes a good point] that &lt;c&gt;pairkeys&lt;/c&gt; may return duplicate "keys", unlike [doc://keys].&lt;/p&gt; </doctext>
